---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, REPO_URL, url } from '../data/site';
---
<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using Maagical, the free, open source Mac menu bar app to read, explain and dictate."
  path="terms/"
  updated="November 5, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to Maagical, the macOS app and this website, published by {PUBLISHER}
    ("we"). By downloading or using Maagical you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <p>
    Maagical is free and open source under the
    <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT License</a>. The license governs your rights to
    the source code; these terms cover using the app we distribute.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Some features use services you connect yourself: ElevenLabs, Groq, Anthropic and Google
    Calendar. You are responsible for your accounts and API keys with those providers, for any
    costs they charge, and for following their terms. Maagical shows estimated costs, but the
    provider's bill is what counts.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Use Maagical lawfully. Do not use it to record or transcribe people without the consent the
    law requires where you are, or to break the terms of the services it connects to.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Maagical is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Speech, transcription and AI
    answers can be wrong; check anything important. To the extent the law allows, we are not
    liable for any damages arising from using the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>How the app handles your data is described in the <a href={url('privacy/')}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms and will post the new version here with a new date. Questions:
    open an issue at <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>github.com/floo-one/vibeflow</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
